      "username": "Powerhound_2000",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/{size}/1859_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-02-08T14:00:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I always thought of reveal as taking all those cards at once keeping in mind the order. At least to me I would think none of them are ever technically the top of the deck until the power or card is finished with it. &nbsp; The only way I see the trap detonating would be if you played Precogoniton and left it on top. However, since this does deal with decks in the SotM app this could be tested out and confirmed. &nbsp; I think the testers for the app can setup specific scenarios and try this. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Edit: app confirms it per Pydro and also tells me I need to dig through Spiff's FAQ&nbsp;</p>",
